## 8. Public Conclusion

Under the measured conditions, the results are **consistent with the hypothesis** that
protocol-compliance failures are not only failures of rule knowledge but also failures
of mandatory verification execution during fluent generation. Raw first-output
compliance converged across groups, while the external gate (E) separated on trigger
activation, unauthorized output, false-pass avoidance and auditability.

